@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+# Summary: `--format markdown`
+
+## Changed
+- `stockreport/report.py`: `render()` accepts `fmt="markdown"`. It renders the same rows and columns as the text report using the vendored tabulate `pipe` style with two-decimal prices, then adds a blank line and `**Total stock value:** <value>`. In the markdown format only, string cells have `|` escaped as `\|` so names cannot break the table. The text format is unchanged.
+- `stockreport/__main__.py`: `--format` now accepts `text` and `markdown`.
+- `tests/test_markdown_escape.py` (new): checks that a `|` in a name is escaped and the table rows keep five unescaped delimiters.
+- `README.md`: documents the `--format markdown` option.
+
+The existing `tests/test_report.py` was not modified. Its markdown tests were already in the repo and failed before this change because the option did not exist.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -m unittest` before the change: 1 failure and 1 error (the two markdown tests). After the change: 4 tests, all pass (`Ran 4 tests ... OK`). This includes the exact-output tests `test_markdown_output` and `test_cli_markdown`.
+- `python -m stockreport inventory.csv --format markdown` prints the expected table and total.
+- Manual check: a name containing `|` without escaping split into extra columns. With escaping, the row keeps its columns.
+
+## Not verified / notes
+- The `|` escaping is my addition, not in the spec. It only applies to the markdown format. It changes nothing for existing data, which has no pipes.
+- Only the vendored tabulate fork was used. I did not check its pipe output against upstream tabulate, and I did not check other characters that GFM treats specially (e.g. backticks or leading `#`). Names with those characters are passed through as-is.
+- Nothing was committed.
+- Nothing outside the allowed paths needed changing.
